31, 2025, one client accounted for 13.7% of the Company&#8217;s total revenues.&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As of December&#160;31, 2024, one vendor accounted
for 13.7% of the Company&#8217;s total accounts payable. As of December&#160;31, 2025, one vendor accounted for 10.2% of the Company&#8217;s
total accounts payable.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the year ended December&#160;31, 2023, no vendor accounted above 10% of the Company&#8217;s total purchases. For the year ended December&#160;31,
2024, one vendor accounted for 14.2% of the Company&#8217;s total purchases. For the year ended December&#160;31, 2025, two vendors accounted
for 12.3% and 12.2% of the Company&#8217;s total purchases, respectively.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b>Off-Balance
