<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">The
Company may be involved in various legal proceedings, claims and other disputes arising from the commercial operations, projects, employees
and other matters which, in general, are subject to uncertainties and in which the outcomes are not predictable. The Company determines
whether an estimated loss from a contingency should be accrued by assessing whether a loss is deemed probable and can be reasonably estimated.
Although the Company can give no assurances about the resolution of pending claims, litigation or other disputes and the effect such outcomes
may have on the Company, the Company believes that any ultimate liability resulting from the outcome of such proceedings, to the extent
not otherwise provided or covered by insurance, will not have a material adverse effect on the Company&#8217;s consolidated financial
position or results of operations or liquidity.</span></p>

